'''''Sedum moranense''''', or '''red stonecrop''', is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Crassulaceae]].<ref name=POWO/>

==Description==
Adult plant has many small green succulent leaves densely clustered around stems.<ref>{{cite web |title=Sedum moranense: complete guide |url=https://gardenworld.app/en/blog/planten/sedum-moranense |website=GardenWorld |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref>

==Habitat and distribution==
Native to Mexico,<ref>{{cite web |title=Sedum moranense (Red Stonecrop) |url=https://worldofsucculents.com/sedum-moranense-red-stonecrop |website=World of Succulents}}</ref> it has also been introduced to Colombia.<ref name=POWO/> It grows primarily in the desert or dry shrubland biome.<ref name=POWO/>

==Taxonomy==
There are two accepted subspecies:<ref name=POWO>{{cite POWO |title=''Sedum moranense'' Kunth |id=275718-1 |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref>
